
NOTE about groups and device permissions:

Add your user to the "video" group to be able to
use the nvidia devices required for 3D to function properly.


NOTE about wayland and eglstream:

If wayland is installed and eglstream support is desired/needed,
additionally install the 'egl-wayland' port.


NOTE about hybrid laptops (Intel iGPU / AMD APU + NVIDIA):

The port installs /etc/modprobe.d/nvidia-hybrid-blacklist.conf. The
integrated-GPU blocks are commented out; uncomment the block matching the
hardware to make the NVIDIA GPU the only display adapter, then run
'dracut --force --regenerate-all' and reboot. See the BLFS book,
chapter 9 ("Hybrid Laptops: Forcing NVIDIA-Only Display"), for details
and verification steps.
